\s1 The Descendants of Reuben
\p \v 1 \w These were the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Reuben|strong="H07205"\w* \w the firstborn|strong="H01060"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*. \w . . .|strong="H03588"\w* \w Though he|strong="H01931"\w* \w was the firstborn|strong="H01060"\w*, \w his birthright|strong="H01062"\w* \w was given|strong="H05414"\w* \w to the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Joseph|strong="H03130"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*, \w because Reuben defiled|strong="H02490"\w* \w his father’s|strong="H00001"\w* \w bed|strong="H03326"\w*. \w So he is not|strong="H03808"\w* \w reckoned|strong="H03187"\w* \w according to birthright|strong="H01062"\w*. \v 2 \w And though|strong="H03588"\w* \w Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w prevailed|strong="H01396"\w* \w over his brothers|strong="H00251"\w* \w and a ruler|strong="H05057"\w* \w came from him|strong="H04480"\w*, \w the birthright|strong="H01062"\w* \w belonged to Joseph|strong="H03130"\w*. \v 3 \w The sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Reuben|strong="H07205"\w*, \w the firstborn|strong="H01060"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w*:
