\li1 \v 20 \w And because|strong="H03588"\w* \w they cried out|strong="H02199"\w* \w to God|strong="H00430"\w* \w in battle|strong="H04421"\w*, \w they were helped|strong="H05826"\w* \w against [their enemies]|strong="H05921"\w*, \w and the Hagrites|strong="H01905"\w* \w and all|strong="H03605"\w* \w their allies|strong="H05973"\w* \w were delivered|strong="H05414"\w* \w into their hands|strong="H03027"\w*. \w Because|strong="H03588"\w* \w they put their trust|strong="H00982"\w* in [God], \w He answered their prayers|strong="H06279"\w*. \v 21 \w They seized|strong="H07617"\w* \w the livestock [of the Hagrites]|strong="H04735"\w*— \w 50,000 {}|strong="H02572"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00505"\w* \w camels|strong="H01581"\w*, \w 250,000 {}|strong="H03967"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02572"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00505"\w* \w sheep|strong="H06629"\w*, \w and 2,000|strong="H00505"\w* \w . . .|strong="H05315"\w* \w donkeys|strong="H02543"\w*. \w [They also took] 100,000|strong="H03967"\w* \w . . .|strong="H00505"\w* \w captives|strong="H00120"\w*, \v 22 \w and|strong="H03588"\w* \w many others|strong="H07227"\w* \w fell|strong="H05307"\w* \w slain|strong="H02491"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w the battle|strong="H04421"\w* \w belonged to God|strong="H00430"\w*. \w And they occupied|strong="H03427"\w* \w the land|strong="H08478"\w* \w until|strong="H05704"\w* \w the exile|strong="H01473"\w*.
\s1 The Half-Tribe of Manasseh
\p \v 23 \w Now the people|strong="H01121"\w* \w of the half-tribe|strong="H02677"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07626"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H04519"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01992"\w* \w were numerous|strong="H07235"\w*. \w They settled|strong="H03427"\w* \w in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w from Bashan|strong="H01316"\w* \w to|strong="H05704"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01179"\w* \w Baal-hermon (that is|strong="H01179"\w*, \w Senir|strong="H08149"\w*, \w [also known as] Mount|strong="H02022"\w* \w Hermon|strong="H02768"\w*).\f + \fr 5:23 \ft Literally \fqa from Bashan to Baal-hermon and Senir and Mount Hermon.\f* \v 24 \w These|strong="H00428"\w* \w were the heads|strong="H07218"\w* \w of their families|strong="H00001"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01004"\w*:
