\li1 \v 26 \w So the God|strong="H00430"\w* \w of Israel|strong="H03478"\w* \w stirred up|strong="H05782"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w the spirit|strong="H07307"\w* \w of Pul|strong="H06322"\w* \w king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H00804"\w* (\w that is|strong="H00853"\w*, \w . . .|strong="H07307"\w* \w vvv|strong="H08407"\w* \w Tiglath-pileser|strong="H08407"\w* \w king|strong="H04428"\w* \w of Assyria|strong="H00804"\w*) \w to take the Reubenites|strong="H07206"\w*, \w the Gadites|strong="H01425"\w*, \w and the half-tribe|strong="H02677"\w* \w . . .|strong="H07626"\w* \w of Manasseh|strong="H04519"\w* \w into exile|strong="H01540"\w*. \w And he brought them|strong="H00935"\w* \w to Halah|strong="H02477"\w*, \w Habor|strong="H02249"\w*, \w Hara|strong="H02024"\w*, \w and the river|strong="H05104"\w* \w of Gozan|strong="H01470"\w*, \w where they remain to|strong="H05704"\w* \w this|strong="H02088"\w* \w day|strong="H03117"\w*.
