\s1 Territories for the Levites
\r (Numbers 35:1–8; Joshua 21:1–45)
\p \v 54 \w Now these [were]|strong="H00428"\w* \w the territories|strong="H01366"\w* \w assigned to the descendants|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Aaron|strong="H00175"\w* \w from the Kohathite|strong="H06956"\w* \w clan|strong="H04940"\w* \w for their settlements|strong="H04186"\w* \w . . .|strong="H02918"\w*, \w because|strong="H03588"\w* \w the first lot|strong="H01486"\w* \w fell|strong="H01961"\w* to them:
\b 
\li1 \v 55 \w They were given|strong="H05414"\w* . . . \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Hebron|strong="H02275"\w* \w in the land|strong="H00776"\w* \w of Judah|strong="H03063"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w and its surrounding|strong="H05439"\w* \w pasturelands|strong="H04054"\w*. \v 56 \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w But the fields|strong="H07704"\w* \w and villages|strong="H02691"\w* \w around the city|strong="H05892"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w were given|strong="H05414"\w* \w to Caleb|strong="H03612"\w* \w son|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Jephunneh|strong="H03312"\w*. \v 57 \w So the descendants|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Aaron|strong="H00175"\w* \w were given|strong="H05414"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Hebron|strong="H02275"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w (a city|strong="H05892"\w* \w of refuge|strong="H04733"\w*), \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Libnah|strong="H03841"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H04054"\w*,\f + \fr 6:57 \ft As in the parallel text at Joshua 21:13; Hebrew \fqa were given the cities of refuge: Hebron, Libnah\f* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Jattir|strong="H03492"\w*, \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Eshtemoa|strong="H00851"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H04054"\w*, \v 58 \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Hilen|strong="H02432"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H04054"\w*,\f + \fr 6:58 \ft Some Hebrew manuscripts; MT \fqa Hilez\ft ; parallel text at Joshua 21:15 \fqa Holon\f* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Debir|strong="H01688"\w* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w -|strong="H04054"\w*, \v 59 \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w Ashan|strong="H06228"\w*,\f + \fr 6:59 \fqa Ashan \ft is a variant of \fqa Ain\ft ; see Joshua 21:16.\f* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w [Juttah,]|strong="H04054"\w*\f + \fr 6:59 \ft Syriac and the parallel text at Joshua 21:16; MT does not include \fqa Juttah,\f* \w -|strong="H00853"\w* \w vvv|strong="H01053"\w* \w and Beth-shemesh|strong="H01053"\w*, \w together with|strong="H00853"\w* \w their pasturelands|strong="H04054"\w*.
\b 
