\li1 \v 10 \w And the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Shimei|strong="H08096"\w*:\f + \fr 23:10 \fqa Shimei \ft was possibly a son or grandson of the \fqa Shimei \ft listed in verse 9.\f* \w Jahath|strong="H03189"\w*, \w Zina|strong="H02126"\w*,\f + \fr 23:10 \ft Most Hebrew manuscripts; one Hebrew manuscript, LXX, and Vulgate (see also verse 11) \fqa Zizah\f* \w Jeush|strong="H03266"\w*, \w and Beriah|strong="H01283"\w*. \w These|strong="H00428"\w* \w [were] the sons|strong="H01121"\w* \w of Shimei|strong="H08096"\w*— \w four [in all]|strong="H00702"\w*. \v 11 \w Jahath|strong="H03189"\w* \w was|strong="H01961"\w* \w the first|strong="H07218"\w* \w and Zizah|strong="H02125"\w* \w was the second|strong="H08145"\w*; \w but Jeush|strong="H03266"\w* \w and Beriah|strong="H01283"\w* \w did not|strong="H03808"\w* \w have many|strong="H07235"\w* \w sons|strong="H01121"\w*, \w so they were counted as|strong="H01961"\w* \w one family|strong="H00001"\w* \w . . .|strong="H01004"\w* \w and received a single|strong="H00259"\w* \w assignment|strong="H06486"\w*.
